        <mxCell id="c135" value="&lt;i&gt;Outlined in coral: the count outside the recorded dates for promotions 1, 4 and 7, which equals their line counts. Outlined in teal: the two lines of promotion 1 outside their scope. Every other count is zero. The window of a promotion whose lines all fail the date test is the calendar months in which they were ordered. Columns B and C, the promotion&#x27;s name and its kind of scope, are hidden.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="441" width="860" height="53" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
